From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:01:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 015/138] ASoC: cs35l33: Fix the boost peak current step check

BST_PEAK_CTL counts 15.625 mA steps above 1.85 A, but the driver checks
that the whole current is a multiple of 15.625 mA. 1.85 A is not one, so
only off-grid values pass and get rounded down. Check the offset from
1.85 A instead. The iPhone 6 value 2.75625 A (0xaa, from iOS) is
rejected today.

TODO before sending: Fixes: tag (driver's initial commit; tree is shallow here)

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
index 8661e6628..8b2a73cbb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
@@ -849,17 +849,16 @@ static int cs35l33_set_bst_ipk(struct snd_soc_component *component, unsigned int
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	if (bst % 15625) {
-		dev_err(component->dev, "Current not a multiple of 15625uA (%d)\n",
+	/* 15.625 mA steps above the 1.85 A minimum */
+	if ((bst - 1850000) % 15625) {
+		dev_err(component->dev,
+			"Current not 1850000uA plus a multiple of 15625uA (%d)\n",
 			bst);
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	while (bst > 1850000) {
-		bst -= 15625;
-		steps++;
-	}
+	steps = (bst - 1850000) / 15625;
 
 	regmap_write(cs35l33->regmap, CS35L33_BST_PEAK_CTL,
 		steps+0x70);
